        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-Level Coding in a 27B Dense Model\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Alibaba's Qwen3.6-27B delivers flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing the previous-generation open-source flagship Qwen3.5-397B-A17B across all major coding benchmarks. The model is 55.6GB compared to 807GB, making it much more accessible. Simon tested it with a quantized version showing outstanding results for a local model.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"open-source LLMs\", \"local models\", \"coding benchmarks\", \"Qwen\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"Firefox 150 includes 271 vulnerability fixes found by Claude Mythos Preview\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Mozilla's CTO Bobby Holley shares their experience applying an early version of Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, resulting in 271 vulnerability fixes in Firefox 150. He notes that 'Defenders finally have a chance to win, decisively' and describes how teams can succeed with focused AI security research.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Bobby Holley (via Simon Willison)\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"AI security\", \"vulnerability detection\", \"Claude Mythos\", \"Firefox\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"Changes to GitHub Copilot Individual plans - Agentic workflows changing compute demands\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"GitHub tightened Copilot usage limits, paused individual plan signups, and restricted Claude Opus 4.7 to the Pro+ plan. The announcement notes that 'Agentic workflows have fundamentally changed Copilot's compute demands' with long-running, parallelized sessions consuming far more resources than the original plan structure was designed to support.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"GitHub Copilot\", \"pricing\", \"coding agents\", \"compute costs\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Is Claude Code going to cost $100/month? Pricing confusion\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Anthropic quietly updated their pricing page to add a $100/month Claude Code option, then reverted it. Simon analyzes the confusing state of Claude Code pricing and compares it to GitHub Copilot's pricing changes in the evolving landscape of AI coding agents.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"pricing\", \"LLM pricing\", \"coding agents\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"ChatGPT Images 2.0 released\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0, their latest image generation model. Sam Altman said the leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 was equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5. Simon tests it with a 'raccoon with a ham radio' prompt to evaluate the model's capabilities.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"image generation\", \"ChatGPT\", \"GPT-image-2\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"llm-openrouter 0.6 released with model refresh\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"Simon released llm-openrouter 0.6 with a new `llm openrouter refresh` command for refreshing the list of available models without waiting for cache to expire. He added this feature to try Kimi 2.6 on OpenRouter as soon as it became available.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"LLM tools\", \"OpenRouter\", \"Kimi\", \"Python\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Claude Token Counter upgraded with model comparisons\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Simon upgraded his Claude Token Counter tool to compare token counts between different models. He found that Claude Opus 4.7's new tokenizer uses 1.46x the number of tokens as Opus 4.6 for the same input, meaning it will be around 40% more expensive despite the same pricing per token.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"tokenization\", \"pricing\", \"Opus 4.7\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Headless everything for personal AI\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Matt Webb and Marc Benioff discuss the rise of 'headless' services designed for AI agents rather than human GUI interaction. Salesforce Headless 360 exposes entire platforms as APIs, MCP, and CLI so AI agents can access data directly. This trend could disrupt per-head SaaS pricing schemes.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-19\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"APIs\", \"SaaS pricing\", \"Salesforce\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→  