     <div class=\"item\">\n   337→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   338→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor: Canvases - Interactive Visualizations</a>\n   339→                        </div>\n   340→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   341→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   342→                            2026-04-15\n   343→                        </div>\n   344→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   345→                            Cursor can now respond by creating interactive canvases with dashboards and custom interfaces built using first-party components like tables, boxes, diagrams, and charts.\n   346→                        </div>\n   347→                    </div>\n   348→\n   349→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   350→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   351→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI 0.34.0: UI Polish and Fixes</a>\n   352→                        </div>\n   353→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   354→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   355→                            2026-04-15\n   356→                        </div>\n   357→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   358→                            April 2026 release featuring UI polish improvements, core fixes, new tools integration, and chat resume footer on session functionality.\n   359→                        </div>\n   360→                    </div>\n   361→\n   362→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   363→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   364→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor: CLI Debug Mode and /btw Support</a>\n   365→                        </div>\n   366→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   367→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   368→                            2026-04-14\n   369→                        </div>\n   370→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   371→                            Quality-of-life improvements to Cursor CLI including /debug for root cause analysis, /btw for side questions without derailing tasks, and /config for interactive settings.\n   372→                        </div>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→\n   375→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   376→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   377→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Model Selection for Agents</a>\n   378→                        </div>\n   379→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   381→                            2026-04-14\n   382→                        </div>\n   383→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   384→                            Model selection improvements for Claude and Codex agents on github.com, giving users more control over AI model choices.\n   385→                        </div>\n   386→                    </div>\n   387→\n   388→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   389→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   390→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Data Residency & FedRAMP</a>\n   391→                        </div>\n   392→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   393→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   394→                            2026-04-13\n   395→                        </div>\n   396→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   397→                            Copilot now offers data residency in US + EU and FedRAMP compliance, addressing enterprise data governance requirements.\n   398→                        </div>\n   399→                    </div>\n   400→\n   401→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   402→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   403→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: BYOK and Local Models</a>\n   404→                        </div>\n   405→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   406→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   407→                            2026-04-07\n   408→                        </div>\n   409→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   410→                            Copilot CLI now supports Bring Your Own Key (BYOK) and local models, giving developers flexibility in model deployment and cost management.\n   411→                        </div>\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→\n   414→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   416→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: SDK in Public Preview</a>\n   417→                        </div>\n   418→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   419→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   420→                            2026-04-02\n   421→                        </div>\n   422→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   423→                            GitHub Copilot SDK is now in public preview, enabling developers to build custom integrations and extensions.\n   424→                        </div>\n   425→                    </div>\n   426→\n   427→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   428→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   429→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: GPT-5.4 Mini in Student</a>\n   430→                        </div>\n   431→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   433→                            2026-04-01\n   434→                        </div>\n   435→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   436→                            GPT-5.4 mini is now available in Copilot Student auto model selection, providing more efficient model options for educational users.\n   437→                        </div>\n   438→                    </div>\n   439→\n   440→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   442→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Cloud Agent Updates</a>\n   443→                        </div>\n   444→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   445→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   446→                            2026-04-01\n   447→                        </div>\n   448→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   449→                            Copilot cloud agent can now research, plan, and code with improved capabilities. Remote control CLI sessions available in public preview on web and mobile.\n   450→                        </div>\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                </section>\n   453→\n   454→                <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   455→                <section class=\"column technical-insights\" id=\"insights\">\n   456→                    <h2 class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   457→\n   458→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   460→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-Level Coding</a>\n   461→                        </div>\n   462→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   463→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   464→                        </div>\n   465→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   466→                            Alibaba's Qwen3.6-27B delivers flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing Qwen3.5-397B-A17B across all major coding benchmarks. 55.6GB vs 807GB model size.\n   467→                        </div>\n   468→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   469→                            <span class=\"tag\">open-source LLMs</span>\n   470→                            <span class=\"tag\">local models</span>\n   471→                            <span class=\"tag\">Qwen</span>\n   472→                        </div>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→\n   475→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   476→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   477→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firefox 150: 271 Vulnerability Fixes</a>\n   478→                        </div>\n   479→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   480→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bobby Holley</a>\n   481→                        </div>\n   482→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   483→                            Mozilla applied Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, resulting in 271 vulnerability fixes. \"Defenders finally have a chance to win, decisively.\"\n   484→                        </div>\n   485→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   486→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n   487→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Mythos</span>\n   488→                            <span class=\"tag\">Firefox</span>\n   489→                        </div>\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→\n   492→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   493→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   494→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot Pricing Changes</a>\n   495→                        </div>\n   496→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   497→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   498→                        </div>\n   499→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   500→                            GitHub tightened Copilot usage limits and restricted Claude Opus 4.7 to Pro+. \"Agentic workflows have fundamentally changed Copilot's compute demands.\"\n   501→                        </div>\n   502→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   503→                            <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n   504→                            <span class=\"tag\">coding agents</span>\n   505→                            <span class=\"tag\">compute costs</span>\n   506→                        </div>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→\n   509→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   510→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   511→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code $100/month Confusion</a>\n   512→                        </div>\n   513→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   514→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   515→                        </div>\n   516→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   517→                            Anthropic quietly added then reverted a $100/month Claude Code option. Analysis of confusing pricing in AI coding agents landscape.\n   518→                        </div>\n   519→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   520→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   521→                            <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n   522→                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM pricing</span>\n   523→                        </div>\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→\n   526→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   527→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   528→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ChatGPT Images 2.0 Released</a>\n   529→                        </div>\n   530→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   531→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   532→                        </div>\n   533→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   534→                            OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0. Altman said leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 was equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5.\n   535→                        </div>\n   536→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   537→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n   538→                            <span class=\"tag\">image generation</span>\n   539→                            <span class=\"tag\">ChatGPT</span>\n   540→                        </div>\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→\n   543→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   544→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   545→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">llm-openrouter 0.6 Released</a>\n   546→                        </div>\n   547→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   548→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   549→                        </div>\n   550→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   551→                            New `llm openrouter refresh` command for refreshing model list without waiting for cache to expire. Added to try Kimi 2.6 on OpenRouter.\n   552→                        </div>\n   553→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   554→                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM tools</span>\n   555→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenRouter</span>\n   556→                            <span class=\"tag\">Python</span>\n   557→                        </div>\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→\n   560→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   561→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   562→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Token Comparison Tool</a>\n   563→                        </div>\n   564→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   565→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   566→                        </div>\n   567→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   568→                            Claude Opus 4.7's tokenizer uses 1.46x the tokens as Opus 4.6 for same input, meaning ~40% more expensive despite same per-token pricing.\n   569→                        </div>\n   570→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   571→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude</span>\n   572→                            <span class=\"tag\">tokenization</span>\n   573→                            <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n   574→                        </div>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→\n   577→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   578→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   579→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Headless Everything for Personal AI</a>\n   580→                        </div>\n   581→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   582→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   583→                        </div>\n   584→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                            Rise of \"headless\" services designed for AI agents rather than human GUI interaction. Could disrupt per-head SaaS pricing schemes.\n   586→                        </div>\n   587→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span>\n   589→                            <span class=\"tag\">APIs</span>\n   590→                            <span class=\"tag\">SaaS pricing</span>\n   591→                        </div>\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→\n   594→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   595→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   596→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude System Prompt Changes</a>\n   597→                        </div>\n   598→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   599→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   600→                        </div>\n   601→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   602→                            Analysis of differences between Claude Opus 4.6 and 4.7 system prompts. Created git timeline tool to browse the changes.\n   603→                        </div>\n   604→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   605→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude</span>\n   606→                            <span class=\"tag\">system prompts</span>\n   607→                            <span class=\"tag\">Anthropic</span>\n   608→                        </div>\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→\n   611→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   612→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   613→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PyCon US 2026 Announced</a>\n   614→                        </div>\n   615→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   616→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   617→                        </div>\n   618→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   619→                            PyCon US 2026 coming May 13-19 in Long Beach, featuring new AI and security tracks this year.\n   620→                        </div>\n   621→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   622→                            <span class=\"tag\">PyCon</span>\n   623→                            <span class=\"tag\">Python</span>\n   624→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n   625→                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   626→                        </div>\n   627→                    </div>\n   628→\n   629→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   630→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   631→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qwen vs Claude: Pelican Benchmark</a>\n   632→                        </div>\n   633→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   634→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Simon Willison</a>\n   635→                        </div>\n   636→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   637→                            Local Qwen3.6-35B-A3B drew a better pelican than Claude Opus 4.7 in the \"pelican riding a bicycle\" benchmark for testing models.\n   638→                        </div>\n   639→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   640→                            <span class=\"tag\">Qwen</span>\n   641→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude</span>\n   642→                            <span class=\"tag\">local LLMs</span>\n   643→                        </div>\n   644→                    </div>\n   645→\n   646→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   647→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   648→                            <a href=\"https://x.com/karpathy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code: First Convincing LLM Agent</a>\n   649→                        </div>\n   650→                        <div class=\"insight-author\">\n   651→                            <a href=\"https://x.com/karpathy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Andrej Karpathy</a>\n   652→                        </div>\n   653→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   654→                            \"The first convincing demonstration of what an LLM Agent looks like\" that lives on your computer. AI programming languages may differ from human conventions.\n   655→                        </div>\n   656→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   657→                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM agents</span>\n   658→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   659→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI-assisted coding</span>\n   660→                        </div>\n   661→                    </div>\n   662→                </section>\n   663→            </div>\n   664→        </div>\n   665→    </main>\n   666→\n   667→    <footer id=\"about\">\n   668→        <div class=\"container\">\n   669→            <a href=\"#\">Guidelines</a>\n   670→            <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n   671→            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n   672→            <a href=\"#\">Legal</a>\n   673→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   674→            <a href=\"#\">Search</a>\n   675→            <br><br>\n   676→            <span style=\"color: #000000;\">AgentDaily - Agentic Coding Research Report</span>\n   677→        </div>\n   678→    </footer>\n   679→</body>\n   680→</html>\n   681→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
