                       <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Remote Control CLI Sessions on Web and Mobile in Public Preview</a>\n   585→                    </div>\n   586→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   587→                        Remote control CLI sessions are now available in public preview on web and mobile, enabling flexible terminal access.\n   588→                    </div>\n   589→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   590→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-13</span>\n   591→                        <span class=\"item-source\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→                </div>\n   594→\n   595→                <div class=\"item\">\n   596→                    <div class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</div>\n   597→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   598→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Version 0.38.0 - Chapters Narrative Flow and Context Compression</a>\n   599→                    </div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   601→                        Released April 14, 2026 featuring Chapters Narrative Flow for intent-based grouping, Context Compression Service, UI Flicker fixes with Terminal Buffer mode, and Persistent Policy Approvals.\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   604→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-14</span>\n   605→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   606→                    </div>\n   607→                </div>\n   608→\n   609→                <div class=\"item\">\n   610→                    <div class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</div>\n   611→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   612→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Version 0.37.0 - Dynamic Sandbox Expansion and Advanced Browser Capabilities</a>\n   613→                    </div>\n   614→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   615→                        Released April 8, 2026 featuring dynamic sandbox expansion and worktree support, Chapters Narrative Flow for better session structure, and enhanced browser agent with persistent sessions.\n   616→                    </div>\n   617→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   618→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-08</span>\n   619→                        <span class=\"item-source\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   620→                    </div>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→            </section>\n   623→\n   624→            <!-- Right Column: Technical Insights -->\n   625→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   626→                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">12 items</span></h2>\n   627→\n   628→                <div class=\"item\">\n   629→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   630→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-Level Coding</a>\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   633→                        Alibaba's Qwen3.6-27B delivers flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing the previous-generation open-source flagship Qwen3.5-397B-A17B across all major coding benchmarks.\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   636→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-22</span>\n   637→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   638→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   639→                    </div>\n   640→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   641→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source LLMs</span>\n   642→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local models</span>\n   643→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Qwen</span>\n   644→                    </div>\n   645→                </div>\n   646→\n   647→                <div class=\"item\">\n   648→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   649→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Firefox 150 includes 271 vulnerability fixes found by Claude Mythos Preview</a>\n   650→                    </div>\n   651→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   652→                        Mozilla's CTO Bobby Holley shares their experience applying an early version of Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, resulting in 271 vulnerability fixes.\n   653→                    </div>\n   654→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   655→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-22</span>\n   656→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   657→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Bobby Holley</span>\n   658→                    </div>\n   659→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   660→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI security</span>\n   661→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude Mythos</span>\n   662→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Firefox</span>\n   663→                    </div>\n   664→                </div>\n   665→\n   666→                <div class=\"item\">\n   667→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   668→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Changes to GitHub Copilot Individual plans</a>\n   669→                    </div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   671→                        GitHub tightened Copilot usage limits, paused individual plan signups, and restricted Claude Opus 4.7 to the Pro+ plan.\n   672→                    </div>\n   673→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   674→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-22</span>\n   675→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   676→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   677→                    </div>\n   678→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   679→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   680→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">pricing</span>\n   681→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">compute costs</span>\n   682→                    </div>\n   683→                </div>\n   684→\n   685→                <div class=\"item\">\n   686→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   687→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Is Claude Code going to cost $100/month?</a>\n   688→                    </div>\n   689→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   690→                        Anthropic quietly updated their pricing page to add a $100/month Claude Code option, then reverted it. Analyzing the confusing state of Claude Code pricing.\n   691→                    </div>\n   692→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   693→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-22</span>\n   694→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   695→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   696→                    </div>\n   697→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   698→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   699→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">pricing</span>\n   700→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding agents</span>\n   701→                    </div>\n   702→                </div>\n   703→\n   704→                <div class=\"item\">\n   705→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   706→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Images 2.0 released</a>\n   707→                    </div>\n   708→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   709→                        OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0, their latest image generation model. Sam Altman said the leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 was equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5.\n   710→                    </div>\n   711→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   712→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-21</span>\n   713→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   714→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   715→                    </div>\n   716→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   717→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">OpenAI</span>\n   718→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">image generation</span>\n   719→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">GPT-image-2</span>\n   720→                    </div>\n   721→                </div>\n   722→\n   723→                <div class=\"item\">\n   724→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   725→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">llm-openrouter 0.6 released with model refresh</a>\n   726→                    </div>\n   727→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   728→                        Simon released llm-openrouter 0.6 with a new `llm openrouter refresh` command for refreshing the list of available models without waiting for cache to expire.\n   729→                    </div>\n   730→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   731→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-20</span>\n   732→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   733→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   734→                    </div>\n   735→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   736→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM tools</span>\n   737→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">OpenRouter</span>\n   738→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Kimi</span>\n   739→                    </div>\n   740→                </div>\n   741→\n   742→                <div class=\"item\">\n   743→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   744→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Token Counter upgraded with model comparisons</a>\n   745→                    </div>\n   746→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   747→                        Simon upgraded his Claude Token Counter tool to compare token counts between different models. Claude Opus 4.7's new tokenizer uses 1.46x the number of tokens as Opus 4.6.\n   748→                    </div>\n   749→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   750→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-20</span>\n   751→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   752→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   753→                    </div>\n   754→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   755→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>\n   756→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">tokenization</span>\n   757→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">pricing</span>\n   758→                    </div>\n   759→                </div>\n   760→\n   761→                <div class=\"item\">\n   762→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   763→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Headless everything for personal AI</a>\n   764→                    </div>\n   765→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   766→                        Matt Webb and Marc Benioff discuss the rise of 'headless' services designed for AI agents rather than human GUI interaction. This trend could disrupt per-head SaaS pricing schemes.\n   767→                    </div>\n   768→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   769→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-19</span>\n   770→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   771→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   772→                    </div>\n   773→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   774→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI agents</span>\n   775→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">APIs</span>\n   776→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">SaaS pricing</span>\n   777→                    </div>\n   778→                </div>\n   779→\n   780→                <div class=\"item\">\n   781→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   782→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Changes in the system prompt between Claude Opus 4.6 and 4.7</a>\n   783→                    </div>\n   784→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   785→                        Anthropic published their system prompts for Claude chat, enabling analysis of how the system prompt evolves. Simon examines the differences between Opus 4.6 and 4.7.\n   786→                    </div>\n   787→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   788→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-18</span>\n   789→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   790→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   791→                    </div>\n   792→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   793→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>\n   794→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">system prompts</span>\n   795→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Anthropic</span>\n   796→                    </div>\n   797→                </div>\n   798→\n   799→                <div class=\"item\">\n   800→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   801→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">PyCon US 2026 in Long Beach with new AI and security tracks</a>\n   802→                    </div>\n   803→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   804→                        PyCon US 2026 is coming May 13-19 in Long Beach, California, featuring new AI and security tracks this year.\n   805→                    </div>\n   806→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   807→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-17</span>\n   808→                        <span class=\"badge announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   809→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   810→                    </div>\n   811→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   812→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">PyCon</span>\n   813→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Python</span>\n   814→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI</span>\n   815→                    </div>\n   816→                </div>\n   817→\n   818→                <div class=\"item\">\n   819→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   820→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen3.6-35B-A3B vs Claude Opus 4.7 - Pelican benchmark</a>\n   821→                    </div>\n   822→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   823→                        Simon compared pelican-drawing capabilities between Alibaba's Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and Anthropic's Claude Opus 4.7, finding that the local Qwen model drew a better pelican.\n   824→                    </div>\n   825→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   826→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-16</span>\n   827→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   828→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Simon Willison</span>\n   829→                    </div>\n   830→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   831→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Qwen</span>\n   832→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>\n   833→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local LLMs</span>\n   834→                    </div>\n   835→                </div>\n   836→\n   837→                <div class=\"item\">\n   838→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   839→                        <a href=\"https://x.com/karpathy\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code and LLM Agents - Practical Coding Experience</a>\n   840→                    </div>\n   841→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   842→                        Andrej Karpathy discusses Claude Code as 'the first convincing demonstration of what an LLM Agent looks like' that lives on your computer.\n   843→                    </div>\n   844→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   845→                        <span class=\"item-date\">2026-04-16</span>\n   846→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   847→                        <span class=\"source-link\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n   848→                    </div>\n   849→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   850→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM agents</span>\n   851→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   852→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI-assisted coding</span>\n   853→                    </div>\n   854→                </div>\n   855→            </section>\n   856→        </main>\n   857→\n   858→        <footer>\n   859→            <p>\n   860→                <strong>Agent Code Daily</strong> — Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Agent SDK</a> |\n   861→                <a href=\"https://github.com/agentdaily\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub</a> |\n   862→                Generated: 2026-04-23\n   863→            </p>\n   864→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 10px;\">\n   865→                Curated daily updates on agentic coding tools, AI development platforms, and technical insights from industry leaders\n   866→            </p>\n   867→        </footer>\n   868→    </div>\n   869→</body>\n   870→</html>"
